    "created_at": "2017-05-02T09:56:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-02T09:56:16Z",
    "body": "`document.activeElement` doesn't become null. `focus` and `blur` would be fired when switching between windows, but changing the focus to address bar also triggers `blur`.\r\n\r\nIf it is not allowed to trigger fullscreen asynchronously, the top level document should always get focused before `requestFullscreen` is called, unless a document from another window requests that.\r\n\r\nSo should we allow a foreground document to put a background document into fullscreen? Given that window cannot raise itself in general, I don't see how allowing that could be useful.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
