    "body": "> So should we allow a foreground document to put a background document into fullscreen? Given that window cannot raise itself in general, I don't see how allowing that could be useful.\r\n\r\nI agree that doesn't sound useful. What should the spec say to prevent that? One thing that might work is a document-bound user gesture concept, so that it's only possible to request fullscreen for the document that was clicked. Is that what you had in mind?",
